  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "e6f072d215d5fce863c599704427ee1b11ef6823",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2299125983,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> New cmake versions warn that install() DESTINATION paths are normalized.\n\nI.e., in CMake 3.31 and later, if [CMP0177](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/policy/CMP0177.html) is `NEW`, \"all `DESTINATION` values given in any form of the `install()` command, except for the `INCLUDES` `DESTINATION` of the `install(TARGETS)` form\" are normalized, and \"The normalization performed is the same as for the `cmake_path()` command (see [Normalization](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/command/cmake_path.html#normalization)).\"\n\nIf the policy isn't set, \"CMake will warn if it detects a path that would be different if normalized, and uses OLD behavior.\"\n\nSo presumably it's warning about paths that would be different if normalized, hence this change...\n\n> This is fixed by explictly normalizing the DESTINATION paths explicitly.\n\n...which uses `cmake_path()` to pre-normalize the path, so that it's normalized regardless of what version of CMake is used and whether, if it's 3.31 or later, policy CMP0177 is unset, set to `OLD`, or set to `NEW`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-01-15T22:30:53.397Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-01-15T22:30:53.397Z",
