          "body": "Bullseye is already oldstable. If someone builds by hand, would using backports be ok? QT6 needs to be pulled from there anyhow. \n\n| release | wireshark | cmake | cmake backports | qt6-base-dev | qt6-base-dev backports |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| Debian Bullseye (oldstable) | 3.4 | 3.18.4 | 3.25.1 | only QT5 | 6.4.2 |\n| Debian Bookworm (stable) | 4.0  | 3.25.1 | 3.31.4 | 6.4.2 | none |\n\n\nUbuntu 20.04 is a bit more difficult as it seems to not have a newer cmake or QT6 in backports. So building the Wireshark master with 20.04 seems a bit difficult - even without bumping cmake. 22.04 and later seem fine however.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
